---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { person, supporters, funding } from '../data/site.js';
import { findPhoto, loadLogos } from '../lib/content.js';

// TODO: content/photos/microct_grapevine.jpg (or .png) with its line in captions.txt.
const microct = findPhoto(/^microct_grapevine\.(jpe?g|png|webp)$/i);
// TODO: logo files in content/logos/ listed in logos.txt. Until then the names show as text.
const logos = loadLogos();
const almond = findPhoto(/^data_almond_vulnerability\./);

const projects = [
  {
    title: 'Reversible collapse and recovery of the xylem',
    text: 'Synchrotron microCT of intact plants through drought and rewatering, with leaf hydraulic conductance and gas exchange measured on the same plants.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Aquaporins and the living pathway',
    text: 'Gene-edited grapevines lacking the aquaporin VvPIP2;1, used to separate the valve from the pipe during dehydration and rehydration.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Dry air and dry soil',
    text: 'Whether the same leaf water potential is equally recoverable when it is reached through dry air or through drying soil.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Water delivery and vascular disease in lettuce',
    text: 'Undergraduate projects on water delivery to inner leaves, tipburn, and Fusarium wilt in the xylem imaged by microCT.',
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="Research"
  description="Caetano Albuquerque, plant physiologist at CSU Monterey Bay: how water transport in plants fails under drought and heat, and whether it recovers."
>
  <h1 class="text-2xl">{person.name}</h1>
  <p class="mt-1 max-w-measure text-muted">
    Plant physiologist. How water transport in plants fails under drought and heat, and whether it recovers.
  </p>

  <div class="mt-8 flex flex-col gap-6 md:flex-row md:items-start">
    <div class="prose-block md:flex-1">
      <p>
        I study how plants respond to drought and recover from it, relating structure and function
        across scales. I combine physiological measurements with synchrotron microCT imaging at the
        Advanced Light Source of the Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory.
      </p>
      <p>
        The standard account of drought damage to the xylem is embolism, and embolism is mostly
        permanent. Using synchrotron microCT in intact grapevines, I found a failure that arrives first
        and reverses. Water-filled conduits collapse before they embolize, and most reopen after
        rewatering, while embolized conduits rarely refill. A collapsed conduit is a kinked garden hose.
        An embolized conduit is a broken pipe.
      </p>
    </div>
    {microct && (
      <figure class="max-w-xs md:w-56 md:shrink-0">
        <Image src={microct.image} alt={microct.caption} widths={[448, 672]} sizes="(min-width: 768px) 14rem, 100vw" class="h-auto w-full" />
        <figcaption class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted">{microct.caption}</figcaption>
      </figure>
    )}
  </div>

  <div class="prose-block mt-4">
    <p>
      My question now is how much of the loss and recovery of leaf water transport under drought each
      of two reversible mechanisms explains: collapse of water-filled xylem conduits, and aquaporin
      control of the living cells. Grapevines lacking the aquaporin VvPIP2;1 kept their stomata open
      longer than wild type as leaves dried, with no change in leaf hydraulic vulnerability, which
      suggests the gene acts on the valve and not on the pipe.
    </p>
    <p>My work has three aims:</p>
    <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-6">
      <li>How different species respond to progressive dehydration, and which traits drive those responses.</li>
      <li>The drought threshold beyond which plants cannot fully recover.</li>
      <li>How dry air and dry soil differ, to understand plant responses to more frequent weather extremes.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-4">
      I choose the plant that best answers the question, from model species to crops such as grapevine
      and lettuce.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 class="section-title">Current projects</h2>
  <dl class="mt-4 max-w-measure space-y-4">
    {projects.map((p) => (
      <div>
        <dt class="font-semibold">{p.title}</dt>
        <dd class="text-muted">{p.text}</dd>
      </div>
    ))}
  </dl>

  {almond && (
    <figure class="mt-6 max-w-lg">
      <Image src={almond.image} alt={almond.caption} widths={[520, 900]} sizes="(min-width: 768px) 32rem, 100vw" class="h-auto w-full border border-rule" />
      <figcaption class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted">{almond.caption}</figcaption>
    </figure>
  )}

  <h2 class="section-title">Earlier work</h2>
  <div class="mt-4 flex max-w-measure gap-4">
    <a href="https://doi.org/10.1093/jxb/eraa392" class="shrink-0 hover:bg-transparent">
      <img src="/img/jxb-2020-cover.webp" width="240" height="313" alt="Cover of Journal of Experimental Botany, volume 71, issue 22, 2020, featuring this paper" class="h-auto w-20 border border-rule" loading="lazy" />
    </a>
    <p>
      In grapevine leaves imaged alive with microCT, leaf hydraulic conductance and gas exchange declined
      early in drought without xylem embolism. The decline was driven by the living cells outside the xylem.
      <a href="https://doi.org/10.1093/jxb/eraa392">Albuquerque et al. 2020, <em>Journal of Experimental Botany</em></a>, journal cover.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 class="section-title">Methods</h2>
  <p class="mt-4 max-w-measure">
    Pressure chamber, porometry and gas exchange, pressure-volume curves, leaf hydraulic conductance by the
    evaporative flux method, optical vulnerability imaging, quantitative anatomy from hand sections,
    synchrotron microCT at beamline 8.3.2 of the Advanced Light Source (Lawrence Berkeley National
    Laboratory), a gravimetric phenotyping platform under construction, and gene-edited grapevine lines
    built with collaborators at UC Davis.
  </p>

  <h2 class="section-title">Funding</h2>
  <h3 class="mt-4 text-base">Research</h3>
  <ul class="mt-2 max-w-measure space-y-3">
    {funding.research.map((g) => (
      <li>
        <span class="font-semibold">{g.funder}.</span> {g.title}. <span class="text-muted">{g.role}, {g.years}.</span>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>
  <h3 class="mt-6 text-base">Teaching</h3>
  <ul class="mt-2 max-w-measure space-y-3">
    {funding.teaching.map((g) => (
      <li>
        <span class="font-semibold">{g.funder}.</span> {g.title}. <span class="text-muted">{g.role}, {g.years}. {g.note}</span>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>
  <h3 class="mt-6 text-base">Synchrotron beamtime</h3>
  <p class="mt-2 max-w-measure">{funding.beamtime}</p>

  {logos.length > 0 && (
    <ul class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-8 gap-y-5">
      {logos.map((l) => (
        <li>
          <a href={l.url} class="block hover:bg-transparent">
            <Image src={l.image} alt={l.org} height={72} class="h-7 w-auto opacity-80 grayscale hover:opacity-100 md:h-9" />
          </a>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  )}
</Base>
